-<section id="source-types">
-<h2>Source Types</h2>
-<p>The marketplace supports three source types for plugins. Each maps
-differently to AI Catalog entry fields:</p>
-<dl>
-<dt>Direct URL source</dt>
-<dd><code>{"source": "url", "url": "https://github.com/org/repo.git", "sha": "..."}</code>
-  maps to entry <code>url</code> pointing at the repository, with <code>sha</code> captured
-  as provenance digest.</dd>
-<dt>Git subdirectory source</dt>
-<dd><code>{"source": "git-subdir", "url": "org/repo", "path": "plugins/name", "ref": "main"}</code>
-  maps to entry <code>url</code> constructed from the repository, path, and ref.</dd>
-<dt>Local path source</dt>
-<dd><code>"./plugins/name"</code> or <code>"./external_plugins/name"</code> maps to entry <code>url</code>
-  pointing at the known repository location for the plugin directory.</dd>
-</dl>
-</section>
